n-to-columbia-university/articleshow/133164017.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-12T00:28:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133164426,imgsize-44508.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Middle East standoff: Why Gulf states may accept that Iran will control the Strait of Hormuz]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133161794.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Gulf energy producers have acknowledged Iran's assertion of control over the critical Strait of Hormuz. This development occurs amidst attempts to resume passage through this essential route, which are stymied by ongoing tensions. Governments in the region prioritize peace over export delays, while Iran aims for financial easing and a prohibition of international warships, extending the disruption of global energy channels.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/middle-east-standoff-why-gulf-states-may-accept-that-iran-will-control-the-strait-of-hormuz/articleshow/133161794.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/middle-east-standoff-why-gulf-states-may-accept-that-iran-will-control-the-strait-of-hormuz/articleshow/133161794.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-11T23:19:16+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133162263,imgsize-194858.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[7-year-old found duct-taped and dead in closet in Cincinnati: Indian-American coroner says she froze for a while when she opened the door]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133161644.cms" /&gt